--- body ---
## Context

The git-erg pre-commit hook template emits, when the erg binary is missing:

    ERROR: erg binary not found. Run 'make build' first.

This is wrong for IDH and any project that vendors the binary at `tickets/erg`:
there is no `make build` here — the binary is committed and refreshed via
`git pull` (or rebuilt from the git-erg source project). 0230 hand-edited the
local copy in `hooks/pre-commit` and `tickets/integration.md`, but the string
also lives in the **vendored binary's template** (`strings tickets/erg` shows
it). Any future `erg install --hooks` re-emits the managed block from that
template and **clobbers the local hand-edit**, reintroducing the stale text.
The durable fix therefore belongs upstream in git-erg, not in IDH.

## Relevant files

- git-erg source: the hook-template string `Run 'make build' first` (and the
  twin "do not commit tickets/erg ... Use 'make build'" line if present).
- IDH `hooks/pre-commit` and `tickets/integration.md` — already hand-edited by
  0230; will be overwritten by `erg install --hooks` until upstream lands.

## Actions

1. In git-erg, locate the hook template string(s) referencing `make build`.
2. Replace with project-agnostic wording, e.g. "erg binary not found. Refresh
   the vendored binary (git pull if committed) or build from the git-erg
   source project." Avoid assuming a `make build` target in the consuming repo.
3. Rebuild the git-erg binary; re-vendor `tickets/erg` into IDH by copying
   git-erg's committed bootstrap binary onto a feature branch and committing it.
   (Correction: IDH's `tickets/erg` is **tracked and hand-committed** — it is
   NOT gitignored and NOT CI-built; CI only runs `erg check`. The original
   "CI rebuilds after merge — do not commit on a feature PR" note was a
   misconception. The binary is refreshed like any tracked file, on a feature
   PR; the 0234 main-commit guard does not block feature-branch commits.)

## Test

- `strings tickets/erg | grep -c "Run 'make build' first"` returns 0.
- `./tickets/erg check tickets/` still passes (the swapped binary is functional).

## Exit criteria

- [x] git-erg hook template no longer says "Run 'make build' first"
      (git-erg ticket 0242, PR #301; rebuilt bootstrap binary 8e825b3).
- [x] `erg install --hooks` in a vendored-binary project no longer reintroduces
      the stale text (the rebuilt binary's embedded template is agnostic).
- [x] IDH re-vendored binary carries the corrected template (this PR;
      `strings tickets/erg` → 0 stale hits, agnostic text present).
